# Project Structure

Svelte 5 + Vite corporate website with an `/admin` console.

## Layout

- `src/pages/site/` — public marketing screens (`/` and future site routes)
- `src/pages/admin/` — admin console screens under `/admin`
- `src/lib/components/` — shared UI components
- `src/lib/<domain>/` — domain logic (e.g. `auth/`)
- `src/lib/utils/` — small shared helpers (`config.js`)
- `src/lib/stores/` — Svelte stores when needed
- `DESIGN.md` + `src/app.css` — design tokens (source of UI values)

Register new routes in `src/App.svelte` with `svelte-routing`.
Keep `/` for the corporate site. Nest every admin screen under `/admin`.
Schema lives in the sibling `innerdial` app (`supabase/migrations/`), not this repo.

## Imports

- Prefer `$lib/...` over deep relative paths into `src/lib`
- Import concrete modules: `$lib/utils/config.js`, not a utils barrel
- Do not add `index.js` files that only re-export other modules
- A feature `index.js` is OK when it owns the public API and contains real logic

```js
// ❌ BAD — re-export-only barrel
export { appConfig } from './config.js';

// ✅ GOOD
import { appConfig } from '$lib/utils/config.js';
```
